# Testing Rules

All **domain logic** must be tested.

Tests live in [`tests/`](tests/) at the project root, mirroring layer folders (`tests/domain/`, `tests/solver/`, etc.). Do not colocate test files inside `src/`.

## Required coverage

- Move correctness tests
- Inverse move tests
- Rotation invariants
- Scramble validity
- Serialization correctness

## Forbidden

- Testing implementation details of React components

## Prefer

- Property-based testing style invariants
- Deterministic tests

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — tests React internals, not cube behavior
it('calls setState when button clicked', () => {
  const setState = vi.fn()
  render(<CubeControls onMove={setState} />)
  fireEvent.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'R' }))
  expect(setState).toHaveBeenCalledWith('R')
})

// ✅ GOOD — invariant: move + inverse restores state
it('applyMove followed by inverse returns solved cube', () => {
  const solved = createSolvedCube()
  const scrambled = applyMoves(solved, scramble)
  const restored = applyMoves(scrambled, inverse(scramble))
  expect(restored).toEqual(solved)
})

// ✅ GOOD — property-style rotation invariant
it.each(allMoves)('move %s preserves sticker count', (move) => {
  const next = applyMove(createSolvedCube(), move)
  expect(countStickers(next)).toBe(54)
})
```

## Core principle

Test **behavior and invariants** in the domain. UI tests should verify user-visible outcomes, not component internals.
